/-!
# [Stacks, Tag 099I]: restriction of scalars along a flat neighbourhood of `ℐ`

Let `𝒞` be a site, `α : 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` a homomorphism of sheaves of commutative rings and `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a
sheaf of ideals of finite type. If `α` is flat and `𝒪/ℐ ≅ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'`, then restriction of scalars
`D(𝒪') ⥤ D(𝒪)` induces an equivalence `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ𝒪') ≌ D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)`.

## Main results

All in the namespace `Stacks.SheafOfModules.DerivedRestrictScalars`:

* `isEquivalence_derivedCompleteRestrictScalars`: [Stacks, Tag 099I].
* `isEquivalence_derivedCompleteRestrictScalars_of_exact`: the same, with flatness given as the
  two exactness instances and the isomorphism as data.
* `isIso_derivedSheafHom_ringModuleMap`: for `Y` derived complete along `ℐ`, the map
  `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪', Y) ⟶ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, Y)` induced by `α` is invertible.

## Implementation notes

The proof is not the source's, which constructs the quasi-inverse `E ↦ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(K ⊗ 𝒪', E)`
from the complex `K ⟶ 𝒪` of [Stacks, Tag 099E] and leaves the verification that it is a
quasi-inverse as "details omitted". Instead:

* `RestrictScalarsEquivalence.lean` reduces the equivalence to the statement that, for every
  complex `K` of `𝒪`-modules and every `Y` derived complete along `ℐ`, precomposition with the
  degreewise extension of scalars `K ⟶ (K ⊗_𝒪 𝒪')_𝒪` is a bijection on maps into `Y`. Its left
  adjoint is derived extension of scalars, which exists because `α` is flat.
* That map is `K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 η` for `η : 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` the map `α` of `𝒪`-modules
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedTensorRingModuleMapArrowIso`), so by the derived currying
  isomorphism of [Stacks, Tag 08J9] it is inverted by `R𝑆heafHom(-, Y)` as soon as `η` is, and then
  precomposition with it is bijective
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.bijective_precomp_of_isIso_derivedSheafHom_map`).
* `R𝑆heafHom(η, Y)` is invertible because it is so after restriction to the slices of a covering
  over which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections
  (`isIso_overDerivedSheafHom_ringModuleMap`), where it is [Stacks, Tag 099H] read through the
  Čech completion of [Stacks, Tag 099B]; invertibility in `D(𝒪)` is local
  (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`).

The hypothesis `𝒪/ℐ ≅ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'` is the invertibility of the canonical map
`quotientMap α ℐ : 𝒪/ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'`; internally it is used in the form [Stacks, Tag 099H] takes,
an isomorphism `𝒪/ℐ ≅ (𝒪 ⊗_𝒪 𝒪')/(ℐ ⊗_𝒪 𝒪')` compatible with `x ↦ x ⊗ 1`
(`exists_quotientIso_of_isIso`). Flatness of `α` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlatMap α`, which is left and right exactness of
`- ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'`. Finite type is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099I](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099I)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099H](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099H)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08J9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08J9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules.DerivedRestrictScalars

open _root_.AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.Sheaves.FlatNeighbourhood (RestrictedRingModule tensorUnitMap tensorUnitComplexMap
  RingModule)

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  [J.HasSheafCompose (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u})]
  [HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  {O O' : Sheaf J CommRingCat.{u}} (α : O ⟶ O')

section Exact

variable [PreservesFiniteLimits
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} O).flip.obj
      (RestrictedRingModule α)))]
  [PreservesFiniteColimits
    (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} O).flip.obj
      (RestrictedRingModule α)))]
  (I : _root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (ringedSite J O).O)))
  (e : cokernel I.ι ≅ cokernel
    ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} O).flip.obj
      (RestrictedRingModule α))).map I.ι))
  (he : cokernel.π I.ι ≫ e.hom = (tensorUnitMap α (RingModule O)).val ≫ cokernel.π
    ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} O).flip.obj
      (RestrictedRingModule α))).map I.ι))

include he in
/-- **`R𝑆heafHom(α, Y)` is invertible for `Y` derived complete along `ℐ`.** Under the hypotheses of
[Stacks, Tag 099I], the map `R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪', Y) ⟶ R𝑆heafHom_𝒪(𝒪, Y)` induced by `α`, read as the
map `η : 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` of `𝒪`-modules, is invertible. It is so on the slices over a covering by
objects over which `ℐ` is generated by finitely many sections
(`isIso_overDerivedSheafHom_ringModuleMap`, through the restriction of derived internal Hom of
[Stacks, Tag 08JB]), and invertibility in `D(𝒪)` is local. -/
theorem isIso_derivedSheafHom_ringModuleMap [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    (Y : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (ringedSite J O).O)))
    (hY : RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (ringedSite J O) I Y) :
    IsIso (((RingedSite.derivedSheafHomBifunctor (ringedSite J O)).map (DerivedCategory.Q.map
      ((HomologicalComplex.single _ (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
        (RingedSite.ringModuleMap (ringedSite J O) α))).op).app Y) := by
  obtain ⟨ι, V, hV, hgen⟩ := (Stacks.SheafOfModules.presheaf_isFiniteType_of_isFiniteType
    I.toSheafOfModules inferInstance).exists_generators
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory hV _ fun k => ?_
  obtain ⟨n, s, hs⟩ := hgen k
  have hnat := (RingedSite.derivedHomRestriction (ringedSite J O) (V k)).natural_left (L := Y)
    (DerivedCategory.Q.map ((HomologicalComplex.single _ (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
        (RingedSite.ringModuleMap (ringedSite J O) α)))
  rw [(Iso.eq_comp_inv _).mpr hnat]
  exact IsIso.comp_isIso' (IsIso.comp_isIso' (Iso.isIso_hom _)
    (isIso_overDerivedSheafHom_ringModuleMap α I e he (V k) s hs Y hY)) (Iso.isIso_inv _)

include he in
/-- **`R𝑆heafHom(-, Y)` inverts the degreewise extension of scalars `K ⟶ K ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'`** for `Y`
derived complete along `ℐ`. That map is `K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 η` up to isomorphism of arrows
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedTensorRingModuleMapArrowIso`), and by the derived currying
isomorphism of [Stacks, Tag 08J9], natural in the middle variable,
`R𝑆heafHom(K ⊗^𝐋_𝒪 η, Y) ≅ R𝑆heafHom(K, R𝑆heafHom(η, Y))`, which is invertible by
`isIso_derivedSheafHom_ringModuleMap`. -/
theorem isIso_derivedSheafHom_tensorUnitComplexMap [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    (K : CochainComplex (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (ringedSite J O).O)) ℤ)
    (Y : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (ringedSite J O).O)))
    (hY : RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (ringedSite J O) I Y) :
    IsIso (((RingedSite.derivedSheafHomBifunctor (ringedSite J O)).map
      (DerivedCategory.Q.map (tensorUnitComplexMap α K)).op).app Y) := by
  have h1 := isIso_derivedSheafHom_ringModuleMap α I e he Y hY
  have hc := RingedSite.derivedCurryIso_natural (ringedSite J O)
    (𝟙 (DerivedCategory.Q.obj K)) (DerivedCategory.Q.map
      ((HomologicalComplex.single _ (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
        (RingedSite.ringModuleMap (ringedSite J O) α))) (𝟙 Y)
  simp only [op_id, CategoryTheory.Functor.map_id, NatTrans.id_app, Category.id_comp,
    Category.comp_id] at hc
  have h2 : IsIso (((RingedSite.derivedSheafHomBifunctor (ringedSite J O)).map
      (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.derivedTensorProductFunctor (ringedSite J O)).obj
        (DerivedCategory.Q.obj K)).map (DerivedCategory.Q.map
          ((HomologicalComplex.single _ (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).map
            (RingedSite.ringModuleMap (ringedSite J O) α)))).op).app Y) := by
    rw [← Iso.inv_comp_eq] at hc
    rw [← hc]
    exact IsIso.comp_isIso' (Iso.isIso_inv _) (IsIso.comp_isIso' (Functor.map_isIso _ _)
      (Iso.isIso_hom _))
  exact isIso_map_op_of_arrow_iso
    ((RingedSite.derivedSheafHomBifunctor (ringedSite J O)).flip.obj Y)
    (RingedSite.derivedTensorRingModuleMapArrowIso (ringedSite J O) α K).symm h2

include he in
/-- **The input of `isEquivalence_derivedCompleteRestrictScalars_of_complexes`, discharged.** For
every complex `K` of `𝒪`-modules and every `Y` derived complete along `ℐ`, precomposition with
the unit `K ⟶ (K ⊗_𝒪 𝒪')_𝒪` of extension of scalars is a bijection on maps into `Y` in `D(𝒪)`.
The unit is `x ↦ x ⊗ 1` (`adjunction_unit_comp_extendRestrictScalarsTensorIso`), which
`R𝑆heafHom(-, Y)` inverts by `isIso_derivedSheafHom_tensorUnitComplexMap`. -/
theorem bijective_precomp_unit [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    (K : CochainComplex (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (ringedSite J O).O)) ℤ)
    (Y : DerivedCategory (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (ringedSite J O).O)))
    (hY : RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} (ringedSite J O) I Y) :
    Function.Bijective (fun g : DerivedCategory.Q.obj
          (((_root_.SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u}
              (ExtendScalarsTensor.ringSheafMap α)).mapHomologicalComplex
            (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj
            (((ExtendScalarsTensor.extendScalarsSheaf α).mapHomologicalComplex
              (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj K)) ⟶ Y =>
        DerivedCategory.Q.map (((ExtendScalarsTensor.adjunction α).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).unit.app K) ≫ g) := by
  refine RingedSite.bijective_precomp_of_isIso_derivedSheafHom_map (ringedSite J O) _ Y ?_
  let eK : ((_root_.SheafOfModules.restrictScalars.{u}
        (ExtendScalarsTensor.ringSheafMap α)).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj
        (((ExtendScalarsTensor.extendScalarsSheaf α).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj K) ≅
      ((((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.sheafTensor.{u, u, u, u, u} O).flip.obj
          (RestrictedRingModule α))).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj K :=
    HomologicalComplex.Hom.isoOfComponents
      (fun p => (ExtendScalarsTensor.extendRestrictScalarsTensorIso α).app (K.X p))
      (fun p q _ =>
        ((ExtendScalarsTensor.extendRestrictScalarsTensorIso α).hom.naturality (K.d p q)).symm)
  have hu : ((ExtendScalarsTensor.adjunction α).mapHomologicalComplex
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).unit.app K ≫ eK.hom = tensorUnitComplexMap α K :=
    HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun p =>
      ExtendScalarsTensor.adjunction_unit_comp_extendRestrictScalarsTensorIso α (K.X p)
  refine isIso_map_op_of_arrow_iso
    ((RingedSite.derivedSheafHomBifunctor (ringedSite J O)).flip.obj Y)
    (f := Arrow.mk (DerivedCategory.Q.map (((ExtendScalarsTensor.adjunction α).mapHomologicalComplex
          (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).unit.app K)))
    (g := Arrow.mk (DerivedCategory.Q.map (tensorUnitComplexMap α K)))
    (Arrow.isoMk (Iso.refl _) (DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso eK) ?_)
    (isIso_derivedSheafHom_tensorUnitComplexMap α I e he K Y hY)
  dsimp only [Arrow.mk_hom, Iso.refl_hom, Functor.mapIso_hom]
  rw [Category.id_comp, ← Functor.map_comp, hu]

include he in
/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099I], with flatness as left and right exactness of `- ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'`.** Let `𝒞`
be a site, `α : 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` a homomorphism of sheaves of commutative rings and `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a sheaf of
ideals of finite type. If `α` is flat — `- ⊗_𝒪 𝒪'` is left and right exact — and
`𝒪/ℐ ≅ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'` — an isomorphism `e : 𝒪/ℐ ≅ (𝒪 ⊗_𝒪 𝒪')/(ℐ ⊗_𝒪 𝒪')` compatible with
`x ↦ x ⊗ 1` — then the functor `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ𝒪') ⥤ D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)` induced by restriction of scalars
`D(𝒪') ⥤ D(𝒪)` (`derivedCompleteRestrictScalars`) is an equivalence. -/
theorem isEquivalence_derivedCompleteRestrictScalars_of_exact [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType] :
    (derivedCompleteRestrictScalars α I).IsEquivalence :=
  isEquivalence_derivedCompleteRestrictScalars_of_complexes α I fun K Y hY =>
    bijective_precomp_unit α I e he K Y hY

end Exact

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 099I].** Let `𝒞` be a site, `α : 𝒪 ⟶ 𝒪'` a homomorphism of sheaves of
commutative rings and `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` a sheaf of ideals of finite type. If `α` is flat and
`𝒪/ℐ ≅ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'`, then restriction of scalars `D(𝒪') ⥤ D(𝒪)` induces an equivalence
`D_comp(𝒪', ℐ𝒪') ⥤ D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)`: the functor `derivedCompleteRestrictScalars α ℐ` is an
equivalence.

Flatness is `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlatMap α` ([Stacks, Tag 03ER]): `𝒪'` is a flat
`𝒪`-module. The isomorphism `𝒪/ℐ ≅ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'` is the canonical map
`quotientMap α ℐ : 𝒪/ℐ ⟶ 𝒪'/ℐ𝒪'` induced by `α` being invertible, with `ℐ𝒪'` the ideal sheaf
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.extendIdeal` of `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ𝒪')`. Finite type is Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`. -/
@[stacks 099I]
theorem isEquivalence_derivedCompleteRestrictScalars
    (hflat : AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlatMap α)
    (I : _root_.SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u} (ringedSite J O).O)))
    [I.toSheafOfModules.IsFiniteType]
    (hquot : IsIso (quotientMap α I)) :
    (derivedCompleteRestrictScalars α I).IsEquivalence := by
  obtain ⟨_, _⟩ := (exactFunctor_iff _).mp hflat
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := exists_quotientIso_of_isIso α I hquot
  exact isEquivalence_derivedCompleteRestrictScalars_of_exact α I e he

end Stacks.SheafOfModules.DerivedRestrictScalars

end
